      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This paper reports our experience of the use of polythene sheet as a temporary dressing for excised wounds. A prospective randomised double-blind trial was conducted to see whether or not polythene dressing was less painful to remove than our traditional dressing of Jelonet. Polythene was found to be less painful (p less than 0.01). Other advantages of the use of polythene are presented."},
